WEBVTT

00:02:29.697 --> 00:02:31.730
Enter quantum computing.

00:02:32.363 --> 00:02:34.563
Quantum computers like this one

00:02:34.597 --> 00:02:37.297
promise to address the atomic limitation

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:41.063
by exploiting subatomic
physical properties

00:02:41.097 --> 00:02:44.030
that weren't even known to man
a hundred years ago.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.230
How does it work?

00:02:45.263 --> 00:02:49.530
Quantum computing enables
a departure from two major constraints

00:02:49.563 --> 00:02:51.663
of classical semiconductor computing.

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:54.297
Classical computers
operate deterministically:

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:59.063
everything is either yes or no,
on or off, with no in between.

00:02:59.063 --> 00:03:03.530
They also operate serially;
they can only do one thing at a time.